---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
import ApiReference from '../../components/ApiReference.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Select"
  description="An accessible select web component built on the native select, with a label, hint, placeholder, and validation."
>
  <h1>Select</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A dropdown built on the native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>: keyboard support, type-to-search,
    mobile pickers, and screen reader announcements all come from the platform. Put{' '}
    <code>&lt;option&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;optgroup&gt;</code> elements inside.
  </p>

  <h2>Basic</h2>
  <Example
    stack
    code={`<elo-select label="Role" hint="Controls what this person can change.">
  <option value="admin">Admin</option>
  <option value="editor" selected>Editor</option>
  <option value="viewer">Viewer</option>
</elo-select>`}
  />

  <h2>Placeholder and required</h2>
  <p>
    A placeholder adds an empty first option, so <code>required</code> blocks submission until the
    user picks.
  </p>
  <Example
    stack
    code={`<elo-select label="Region" placeholder="Choose a region" required>
  <optgroup label="Americas">
    <option value="us-east">US East</option>
    <option value="us-west">US West</option>
  </optgroup>
  <optgroup label="Europe">
    <option value="eu-west">EU West</option>
  </optgroup>
</elo-select>`}
  />

  <h2>Keyboard</h2>
  <p>
    Arrow keys, typing to jump to an option, and opening the list all follow the native select on
    each platform.
  </p>

  <h2>API</h2>
  <ApiReference tag="elo-select" />
</Docs>
